# Issue: CType's hash-cons table previously returned canonical nodes holding
# the positions of whichever file first constructed each ground type, leaking
# sibling-file positions into .bo signatures in a `bsc -u` batch.
# Fix: canonical nodes are position-free values (GroundCType included) and
# constructors return occurrence spines carrying the caller's own positions.
# Probe: PosOrder writes ground types that PosOrderScramble builds first in
# the batch; its .bo dump, hash included, must match a one-shot compile and
# remain invariant under -trace-intern-reverse.

batching_bo_pair PosOrder.bs PosOrderRoot.bs PosOrderScramble.bs
reverse_intern_same_bo PosOrder.bs
